WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.340
Did the hospital [Memorial Medical Center] have a contingency plan for that kind of storm?

2
00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:07.000
Stocking up supplies?

3
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.480
Well, I think it happened so fast.

4
00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.000
Our cafeteria's in the basement.

5
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.360
So we ran out of food the minute the water came up.

6
00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:19.060
I think we just avoided that bullet all them years, and this one caught us.

7
00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:20.620
And I think we were hoping to avoid.

8
00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:28.680
Because I had worked on a book on Charity Hospital during Katrina, and they had stockpiled some food and water and that kind of thing.

9
00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:30.540
But that . . . the hospital administration . . .

10
00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:34.720
You would like to think that we had water stocked somewhere.

11
00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:40.180
But it makes me wonder, given that by Monday we were out of food and water.

12
00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:41.660
So where was it?

13
00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:43.520
Yeah.

14
00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.040
What about generators and power?

15
00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:47.860
Generators were under water.

16
00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:49.380
So they had no power.

17
00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:52.640
And I'm sure I'll get to how we evacuated the patients.

18
00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:57.580
And I'll tell you about how that came to hurt us, with the power.

19
00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:06.460
But yeah, our generators were in the basement/first floor area, so it was like having none.

20
00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:07.560
Were you afraid to stay?

21
00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:09.020
How did you feel about staying?

22
00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:12.100
I was of course uncomfortable to stay, yes.

23
00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:15.220
But I was always uncomfortable to stay.

24
00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:17.480
It wasn't like Katrina was different.

25
00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:21.060
I was always cautious because I had kids.

26
00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:27.480
I didn't ever take the kids with me because I don't think that's a situation kids should be put in, if I can do anything else.

27
00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.100
Because it gets dangerous.

28
00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:32.600
You've got to think, you've got people who are going to be without medicines.

29
00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:35.920
You have drug addicts on the street who live around the corner.

30
00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:38.740
And we have what they need in a time when they can't get it.

31
00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:40.040
So you always going to know,

32
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:44.520
these people are going to come in and do what they need to do to get what they need to get.

33
00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:46.060
So you don't want kids there.

34
00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:50.340
You don't want yourself in that situation, but, I mean, I had to be there.

35
00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:52.520
So you make the best of it, and you try and do the best you can.
